{
  "final_quality": "tie",
  "reason": "Both plans support the same consequential outcome: a bounded, standard-library normalized substring scan over the application connection, preserving original titles, distinct IDs and ID order. Both cover the required positive, negative and empty-query cases, explicitly supply missing caller/table setup, and retain implementation, regression and consumer acceptance as future work. Neither depends on unverified FTS5 semantics. Differences in normalization policy, test detail and review effort do not demonstrate a better outcome for the stated requirements.",
  "decisive_evidence": [
    {
      "side": "A",
      "quote": "Normalization policy: NFD, casefold, NFD again, remove Unicode mark categories M*. Apply identically to titles and query.",
      "locator": "A.planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "consequence": "The explicit local algorithm supports accent removal, casefold expansion and interior substring matching without changing displayed titles."
    },
    {
      "side": "B",
      "quote": "Planned private key(value): value.casefold(), NFD normalize, remove characters with Unicode category Mn; apply identically to titles and query.",
      "locator": "B.planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "consequence": "B likewise specifies a sufficient algorithm for the required examples; its adjacent empty-query guard prevents match-all behavior."
    },
    {
      "side": "A",
      "quote": "Read SELECT id,title FROM catalog ORDER BY id through that connection.",
      "locator": "A.planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "consequence": "Application-owned retrieval and ordered filtering preserve the connection boundary and deterministic identity ordering; the following contract returns original tuples."
    },
    {
      "side": "B",
      "quote": "Caller owns connection, table setup, transactions and close.",
      "locator": "B.planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, Interfaces and boundaries",
      "consequence": "Missing initialization is explicitly assigned rather than assumed to exist, with read-only search and consumer setup retained in W1."
    },
    {
      "side": "A",
      "quote": "Product and consumer acceptance remain due after implementation",
      "locator": "A.plans[0].final.summary",
      "consequence": "Observed feasibility and the passing connection baseline are not promoted into feature acceptance."
    },
    {
      "side": "B",
      "quote": "This procedure is NOT-REPLAYED against product: src.search is absent.",
      "locator": "B.planning_artifacts: docs/shiploop/architecture.md, RB-2",
      "consequence": "The public consumer remains an explicit future obligation despite the successful disposable probe."
    },
    {
      "side": "B",
      "quote": "Changed: environment.md specifies rows 4/5, exact ordered IDs, literal wildcard results and a newly inserted beacon row 6.",
      "locator": "B.planning_artifacts: .shiploop-improve/test-strategy-8ea10021/reviews/review-1.md",
      "consequence": "Earlier review materially strengthened future acceptance oracles before the initial plan; this is useful rework, not evidence of superior final quality."
    }
  ],
  "initial_plan_and_rework": "Both submitted initial plans already contain supported mechanisms, prerequisite ordering and future acceptance ownership, and both final plan records are unchanged. A's retained reviews report no material correction. B's earlier test-strategy review corrected underspecified decomposed-title and wildcard expectations and added a fresh-row control, followed by a satisfactory review. That correction matters to acceptance quality, but it preceded the initial plan and did not change the chosen mechanism. Neither final plan review demonstrates consequential rework.",
  "earlier_evidence_value": "Source inspection established the connect-only application, JSON seed and absent loader/consumer. Earlier boundary observations supported ordered retrieval, the normalized scan, required results and the 5000-row workload; raw LIKE failed required matching. Reusing this evidence was legitimate because product sources remained unchanged. Another experiment was unnecessary to establish the same mechanism or certify a future implementation. FTS5 remained untested and unselected. API/schema defaults were owned planning decisions, while external boundaries were outside the requested scope and unverified.",
  "harms_or_lost_requirements": [
    "No demonstrated material harm or lost requirement in either final plan. A Python consumer is sufficient because the request does not require a CLI.",
    "Reported redundant commands represent possible investigation cost, without a demonstrated correctness regression. No retained disposable scratch artifact is shown to compromise experiment validity, authority, sensitive data or running resources."
  ],
  "individual_judgment_corrections": [
    "B's empty decision_rework list is accurate for initial-to-final plan review, but would be incomplete as a claim about all review work: test-strategy review-1 explicitly records a material test-contract correction. Its evidence_timing section already acknowledges that earlier change.",
    "No substantive factual error in either judgment's assessment of the final mechanism or pending implementation acceptance is established by the retained records. The event-specific claims about redundant commands require the omitted raw transcript for independent verification."
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "limits": [
    "Neither outcome includes implemented search, durable feature-test results or executed public-consumer acceptance; this is planning quality, not release readiness.",
    "The full probe scripts and raw command transcript are not reproduced here. Probe apparatus, exact invocation history and claimed command redundancy cannot be independently audited from the retained accounts alone.",
    "A's investigation accounting is expressly estimated; elapsed session time and extra review activity do not establish comparative efficiency or a general improvement in this small diagnostic pilot."
  ]
}
